{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into a perception plant (G1) and a motion plant (G2). G1 models all possible sensor outcomes as uncontrollable events. G2 models the robot's motion commands as controllable events. The specifications (E1-E4) bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Recovery from obstacles uses short directed turns and only escalates to full_rotate after repeated failures. move_backward is used only as a brief escape from front obstacles. Exploration is biased toward forward/random_walk when clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plants for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specifications bind perception to safe actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors, with strong bias toward forward progress."
  ],
